venue/src/interfaces/AggregatorV3Interface.sol

    Chainlink's data feed interface, MIT, copyright SmartContract Chainlink
    Limited SEZC, from the npm package "chainlink slash contracts", file
    src/v0.8/shared/interfaces/AggregatorV3Interface.sol. Vendored verbatim:
    five function signatures, unmodified, with a header naming the source. The
    package is not installed; copying one interface is smaller than adding a
    dependency tree to a Foundry project that has one submodule.

    It is used in both directions and that is deliberate.

    venue/src/oracle/PrimeOracle.sol IMPLEMENTS it, so the venue's own clean
    price is readable by anything that already speaks Chainlink, and

    venue/src/oracle/PrimeOracle.sol CONSUMES it on its cash-leg seat, which is
    a governed address rather than a constant.

    That seat does NOT hold a Chainlink aggregator on Hedera, and the reason is
    recorded rather than glossed. Chainlink's feeds here are access controlled:
    a contract reading one gets `No access`, while decimals() answers anyone.
    Measured on testnet and mainnet, all seven feeds, in
    probes/chainlink-hedera.out. No Chainlink contract is called by any deployed
    contract in this project. Only the interface above is used, and only the
    seven addresses are named, in documentation and in a probe.

    Nothing about Chainlink's aggregation, operator set, or off-chain reporting
    is this project's work, and this project makes no claim to integrate with it
    on this chain beyond the interface it borrows.

venue/src/interfaces/IExchangeRate.sol

    Hedera's exchange rate system contract interface, HIP-475, Apache 2.0,
    copyright Hedera Hashgraph LLC and the Hiero contributors, from the
    hedera-smart-contracts repository. Two function signatures, unmodified.

    The contract behind it lives at 0x168 and is the network's, not ours. It is
    what every transaction fee on Hedera is priced at.
    venue/src/oracle/HederaRateFeed.sol is our thin adapter that presents it in
    AggregatorV3Interface's shape; the rate itself is Hedera's.

venue/src/interfaces/ICashToken.sol

    Not vendored, and listed here so the absence is on the record rather than
    assumed. The three signatures are EIP-20's, which is a public specification
    and not code under copyright, and the file is written here rather than
    copied from any implementation: three functions out of the standard's
    nine, no allowance model, and a header saying why.

    What sits behind it on chain is the ERC-20 facade that Hedera Token Service
    exposes for a fungible token. That facade is the network's and not ours, in
    the same relationship as 0x168 above. The paying agent's charge is a
    fractional custom fee on the token's own HTS fee schedule, collected by the
    network during the transfer, so no fee arithmetic in this repository is
    involved and none is claimed.

